= Voltage — Simple =

'''Voltage''' is the difference in electrical potential between two points. You can think of it as how much electric potential energy changes for each unit of charge.

A voltmeter measures voltage between two points. A battery can have voltage across its terminals even when no circuit is connected.

Voltage is different from [[Electric current|current]], which describes how much charge moves each second. A circuit's current depends on its electrical components, including [[Resistor|resistors]].

